<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks fall.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks fall.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			 3/4/97		   3/4/97	     12/4/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    575			600	     500-525</p>
<p>    Naphtha	   50-75			 75		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,700-1,750	    1,750-1,800		 1,700</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    325		  300-325		   275</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     10		    10-15		    10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks dipped during reasonable active movement of small quantities, including a few outgoing cargoes and some barges departing for Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks dipped as product left for the chemical sector and the gasoline pool.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks fell despite the arrival of some product, including low sulphur material, from Russia. Rhine, Benelux and French markets absorbed diesel and some heating oil.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks changed little. Not much new product arrived by cargo.</p>
<p>Some jet fuel left for the aviation sector.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
